35bfe244f9e91639f2b5","event_uuid":"16cc068a-48e5-4eaa-865b-8ce8a4767ef0","position":{"commit_sha":"eeff66fbfd3cb41eee8d8cebdf5d8b60020491aa","position":"1795406757915046001-16cc068a-48e5-4eaa-865b-8ce8a4767ef0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"92065cc1a829dfb076502c4d297d0671a37dca95dd3274db4bd8658f3825b0a6","event_uuid":"c0bddaeb-09de-4ee9-a42d-36997fbb0fd7","position":{"commit_sha":"ef50707890979205260b0c789f98ed98dc5b1f90","position":"1795407481393858001-c0bddaeb-09de-4ee9-a42d-36997fbb0fd7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"05f74084-8156-4489-b43f-fbb9222cdc20","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root-cause evidence (2026-11-22 18:20 PST): box git is 2.47.3 with maintenance.autoDetach; MCP container rebar-mcp-13d4a73cde21-8092 had 3 'Zs [git] <defunct>' + 1 '[mcp-entrypoint.] <defunct>' children of PID 1 (rebar-mcp) since boot at 17:52 PST; review-bot (restarted 17:54 PST) had 0 with no reviews since. No container has HostConfig.Init. Local repro (git 2.53, PID 1 = sleep): each git commit/fetch leaves one 'Zs [git] <defunct>' via 'git maintenance run --auto --quiet --detach' (GIT_TRACE); 200 zombies from 200 commits; under docker run --init: 0. Plan in description.","timestamp":1795400839222197001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review PASS (signed at 13d4a73cde2). Claimed. Advisory follow-ups: box has /usr/bin/docker-init (tini de40ad0, Docker 25.0.16, compose v2.32.4) so init: true / --init resolve there. A 3rd raw-fetch path also feeds the zombies: review_bot/gerrit_client.py clone_change_ref (git fetch --depth 2 without maintenance suppression). Gerrit and opcert get init only at their next compose-up (autodeploy recreates review-bot and MCP only); AC2 is measured over all processes in the review-bot container's pid namespace, since after the fix orphans re-parent to docker-init, not uvicorn.","timestamp":1795401987307397001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AC1 box evidence (read-only ps sampler over the review-bot container, PID 1 = uvicorn pid 1306522, 2026-11-22 19:32-20:02 PST, during the review of change 3529; git 2.47.3). Two call paths leave the `[git] <defunct>` children:\n1. Raw `git fetch` with git's default maintenance settings daemonizes `git maintenance run --auto --detach`. 19:32:30 a `Zs [git] <defunct>` (own session) appeared right after `gerrit_client.clone_change_ref`'s `git -C .../reviewbot-<x> fetch -q --depth 2`; 19:32:53 two more after the per-review clone's tickets fetch.\n2. The tickets store's post-commit foreground `git maintenance run --auto --quiet --task=commit-graph --task=loose-objects --task=incremental-repack` (direct child of uvicorn, own session) ran into its 120 s bound on every commit: 19:39:24 -> 19:41:25, 19:41:28 -> 19:43:28, 19:43:31 -> 19:45:31, 19:45:34 -> 19:47:35. Each time the reap killed the group and its child git (same session id as the maintenance process) was left as `Z [git] <defunct>` re-parented to PID 1. The 120 s maintenance timeouts are the \"git maintenance timeouts\" already counted under newrich-discreet-nettlefish.\nAlso seen: one transient `Zs [python] <defunct>` from the detached snapshot gc_trigger (uvicorn's own child; Python reaps it at the next Popen). Zombies under PID 1 at 20:02 PST: 8.\nBoth git paths end in an orphan re-parented to PID 1, which init: true / --init (change 3529) reaps. Separately filed: antiviral-agrarian-amurminnow (the sample showed the bot's Gerrit password in a git fetch argv; redacted from the saved sample).","timestamp":1795406716107693001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Change 3529 merged 2026-11-22 20:05 PST as 391b0608096 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, make verify rc=0: 21832 + 231 passed). Waiting on the merge-triggered autodeploy to recreate review-bot and MCP.","timestamp":1795406757915046001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Post-deploy (2026-11-22 20:17 PST): autodeploy recreated compose-review-bot-1 at 20:07:04 PST and rebar-mcp-391b06080962-8093 at 20:08:02 PST; both HostConfig.Init=true with PID 1 /sbin/docker-init. Zombies across each container's whole process list: review-bot 0, MCP 0 (the previous MCP container had 4 from boot, incl. the provisioning subshell). opcert and gerrit still Init=nil until their next compose-up (expected). No review has run on the new review-bot yet; next check is during the review of the bug 2 change.","timestamp":1795407481393858001}],"created_at":1795396440172915001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0bb89129-64af-4919-baa7-6245316fe7cf","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"688f-060e-c96c-4484"},{"link_uuid":"16a46f57-89d2-40e3-b20f-f85f6b890508","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8983-a808-7ad5-4d20"},{"link_uuid":"7c778487-c975-406d-becd-f1eec0d047ae","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4c3c-6528-109a-40f6"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nOn 2026-11-22 at 17:12 PST the review-bot process (pid 1254853 on i-00880b2c7f13527c5, container started 16:20 PST) had 17 `[git] <defunct>` children, aged 0-47 minutes. uvicorn is the container's PID 1 (`infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` sets no `init:` for `review-bot`, and `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` passes no `--init`), so git processes orphaned inside the container are re-parented to it and never reaped. Each zombie holds a pid-table slot until the container is recreated. Found while investigating newrich-discreet-nettlefish; it is not the cause of the review stalls.\n\nNot yet established: which call path orphans these git processes (candidates: subprocess timeouts that kill only the parent, the snapshot `gc_trigger` detached child, git's own auto-maintenance children).\n\n## Findings (root cause)\n- Every `git commit`, `git fetch` and `git merge` on the box's git (2.47.3, which carries `maintenance.autoDetach`) runs `git maintenance run --auto --quiet --detach`. That child forks, its parent exits, and the daemonized `git` calls `setsid()`. The orphan is re-parented to the container's PID 1 and becomes a `Zs [git] <defunct>` when it exits. Reproduced locally (git 2.53 container, PID 1 = `sleep`): 1 zombie per commit/fetch, 200 after 200 commits; `GIT_TRACE=1` shows the `maintenance run --auto --quiet --detach` spawn. The same workload under `docker run --init` left 0 zombies.\n- Review-bot path: `rebar._snapshot.git_fetch.fetch_origin` and `repo_snapshot` run raw `subprocess.run([\"git\", ..., \"fetch\", ...])`, which do not get the store's implicit-maintenance suppression (`gitutil._without_implicit_maintenance`), and per-review clones carry no `maintenance.autoDetach=false`. The tickets clone already sets both autoDetach keys false.\n- On 2026-11-22 at 18:20 PST the MCP container `rebar-mcp-13d4a73cde21-8092` (PID 1 = `rebar-mcp`, started 17:52 PST) had 3 `Zs [git] <defunct>` plus 1 `[mcp-entrypoint.] <defunct>` (the `provision_store &` subshell, whose parent is the exec'd server), all from boot. opcert and gerrit had 0. None of the 4 containers runs an init (`docker inspect` HostConfig.Init = nil).\n\n## Approach\nFix the class at the container boundary rather than per git call site: an init process as PID 1 reaps every orphan regardless of which git path daemonized it, including future ones. Docker's bundled `docker-init` (tini) is used through compose `init: true` and `docker run --init`, so no image change and no new dependency. Signals still reach the server: docker-init forwards SIGTERM to its child, so stop-grace drain is unchanged. The MCP entrypoint's provisioning subshell is detached with `( provision_store & )` so it is re-parented to the init and reaped, instead of becoming an unreaped child of the exec'd server.\n\n## Scope\n- `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`: `init: true` on all 4 services (gerrit, review-bot, opcert, mcp).\n- `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`: `--init` in `mcp_run_new`'s `docker run` (blue-green MCP containers are launched outside compose).\n- `infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh`: background provisioning as `( provision_store & )`.\n- `tests/unit/test_container_init_reaper.py` (new): guard test.\n\n## Testing\n- New guard test: every compose service declares `init: true`; the anti-vacuity check pins the service set; `mcp_run_new`'s `docker run` argv carries `--init`; every other `docker run -d` in `infra/scripts/*.sh` carries `--init`; the entrypoint double-forks provisioning. Each assertion is checked against a seeded bad input (a service without `init`, an argv without `--init`) so it cannot pass vacuously.\n- Existing `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py` and `tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py` keep passing.\n- `make verify` before push.\n- Box, after the merge-triggered autodeploy recreates review-bot and MCP: `docker inspect` shows `Init=true`, PID 1 is `docker-init`, and the zombie count among the containers' processes stays 0 across reviews; sampled over a full day for the second criterion.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The call path that leaves the git children is identified with box evidence.\n- [ ] After a fix is deployed, the review-bot process has no `<defunct>` children older than 1 minute across a full day.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","reason":"init: true on every service so an init reaps orphaned git"},{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"--init on the blue-green MCP docker run"},{"path":"infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh","reason":"detach provisioning so the init reaps it"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_container_init_reaper.py","reason":"guard test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","4c3c-6528-109a-40f6"],["relates_to","8983-a808-7ad5-4d20"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"9954126d-e7ce-4922-a811-ef3fef98e917","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"585e-8f49-dff0-4ada","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Review-bot leaves [git] <defunct> zombies: uvicorn runs as the container's PID 1 and never reaps orphaned git children","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f9e9890e-6503-4d8a-aa25-b5b5074bc9eb","0bb89129-64af-4919-baa7-6245316fe7cf","ad66247e-d04c-4130-aef4-bcf238d2eabc","83df6bf4-12eb-47a1-a2bc-b7c47fce611a","f027fe30-30e1-48ce-b8fe-f78d918b4319","16a46f57-89d2-40e3-b20f-f85f6b890508","4c0c713c-434a-4cdf-b90e-4059a75d37d5","9954126d-e7ce-4922-a811-ef3fef98e917","9f57dbf2-0ebc-4c21-a9ea-5f11d69e1bb4","b121d101-bee1-44f4-9e1e-a2555efff390","7c778487-c975-406d-becd-f1eec0d047ae","b1ab0b6d-122f-4eeb-8db9-2820a5204a57","16cc068a-48e5-4eaa-865b-8ce8a4767ef0","c0bddaeb-09de-4ee9-a42d-36997fbb0fd7"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795407481393858002,"uuid":"456bb53d-e146-